{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "underwriting-limits",
  "title": "Mortgage limits at a 700 score",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "965b255e-307a-4b9f-afb5-ed0523cfaa8e",
      "question": "Under the consumer credit policy, what is the maximum debt-to-income ratio and the maximum loan-to-value for a mortgage applicant with a 700 credit score?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-03T04:19:28.337495Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-03T04:19:35.711062Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "Based on the Consumer Credit Policy (version 5.1, effective 1 July 2026), a credit score of 700 falls in the **Good** band (670–719). For that band, the underwriting table specifies:\n\n| Measure | Maximum |\n|---------|---------|\n| Debt-to-Income (DTI) | 40% |\n| Loan-to-Value (mortgage) | 90% |\n\n[1]\n\nThe policy notes that the maximum DTI applies to all three products (personal, auto, mortgage), while the 90% LTV is the mortgage-specific limit (auto LTV is 110% for the same band).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Unstructured Retrieval evidence — consumer_credit_policy.pdf — evidence `hermes-receipt:2b05504270a846bbe36c82cd540f02f9e052f5e21f55f2296f034378841ccb82`",
        "citations": [
          {
            "number": 1,
            "evidenceId": "hermes-receipt:2b05504270a846bbe36c82cd540f02f9e052f5e21f55f2296f034378841ccb82",
            "label": "Unstructured Retrieval evidence — consumer_credit_policy.pdf",
            "capabilityId": "unstructured_retrieval",
            "invocationId": "hermes-tool:chatcmpl-tool-58700617df85454aab6d5613eca74913"
          }
        ]
      },
