                "title": "consumer_credit_policy.pdf",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Consumer Credit Policy\n3.2 Credit score bands, debt-to-income and loan-to-value limits\nDebt-to-income is the borrower’s total monthly debt payments, including the payment on the proposed loan, divided by gross monthly income. The maximum DTI in Table 3 applies to all three products. Loan-to-value is the loan amount divided by the lesser of the purchase price and the appraised value (mortgage) or the retail value in the Bank’s valuation guide (auto). A personal loan has no LTV limit. DTI and the credit band are recorded once, at origination, and are not refreshed during the life of the loan.",
                "metadata": {
                  "parser": "nemotron-parse-2.0",
