                "title": "consumer_credit_policy.pdf",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Consumer Credit Policy\n3.2 Credit score bands, debt-to-income and loan-to-value limits\n3.4 Exceptions\nA loan above the maximum DTI or LTV in Table 3 may be approved only by the regional credit officer, and only when at least two compensating factors are documented: twelve months of liquid reserves, a customer relationship of five years or more, a co-borrower with a credit score in a higher band, or a down payment of at least 20 percent. Approved exceptions may not exceed 5 percent of originations by count in any quarter. Every exception is reported to the Credit Risk Committee with the borrower’s band, the ratio approved and the factors relied on.\nSynthetic document for a software demonstration. Harborview Community Bank is fictional. Page 2\nHARBORVIEW COMMUNITY BANK HCB-CRE-001 | Version 5.1",
