                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Consumer Credit Policy\n8. Revision history\nVersion 5.1 lowered the maximum DTI for every credit band by between 2 and 6 percentage points. Table 5 compares the new limits with those of version 5.0, which applied to applications taken from 1 July 2025 through 30 June 2026.\nExceptional, Maximum DTI, version 5.0 = 48%. Exceptional, Maximum DTI, version 5.1 (current) = 45%. Exceptional, Change = -3 points. Very Good, Maximum DTI, version 5.0 = 45%. Very Good, Maximum DTI, version 5.1 (current) = 43%. Very Good, Change = -2 points. Good, Maximum DTI, version 5.0 = 43%. Good, Maximum DTI, version 5.1 (current) = 40%. Good, Change = -3 points. Fair, Maximum DTI, version 5.0 = 40%. Fair, Maximum DTI, version 5.1 (current) = 36%. Fair, Change = -4 points. Poor, Maximum DTI, version 5.0 = 36%. Poor, Maximum DTI, version 5.1 (current) = 30%. Poor, Change = -6 points\nTable 5. Maximum DTI, version 5.1 against the version 5.0 limits it replaced\n4.8, Effective = 1 January 2024. 4.8, Summary of change = Annual review; no limit changes. 5.0, Effective = 1 July 2025. 5.0, Summary of change = Added the hardship and loan modification section; raised the Exceptional-band mortgage LTV. 5.1, Effective = 1 July 2026. 5.1, Summary of change = Lowered maximum DTI in every band (Table 5); added the monitoring of recent originations in section 7\nTable 6. Policy versions\nSynthetic document for a software demonstration. Harborview Community Bank is fictional. Page 4",
