                "title": "consumer_credit_policy.pdf",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Consumer Credit Policy\n2. Governance and approval authority\nThe Board Credit Committee approves this policy once a year and whenever a limit in section 3 changes. The Chief Credit Officer owns the policy and reports exceptions, delinquency and charge-offs to the Credit Risk Committee every quarter.\nCredit decisions are made within the authority shown in Table 1. Authority is set by the total of the loan being approved plus all other credit the borrower already has with the Bank. A lender may never approve a loan for a relative, an employee reporting to the lender or a business the lender owns.\nBranch lender, Personal loans (unsecured) = Up to $15,000. Branch lender, Auto loans = Up to $40,000. Branch lender, Mortgages = Not authorized. Regional credit officer, Personal loans (unsecured) = Up to $35,000. Regional credit officer, Auto loans = Up to $75,000. Regional credit officer, Mortgages = Up to $400,000. Credit Committee, Personal loans (unsecured) = $35,001 to $50,000. Credit Committee, Auto loans = Not applicable. Credit Committee, Mortgages = $400,001 to $750,000\nTable 1. Lending authority by approver",
